<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gök Madrasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1271">1271</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Gök Medrese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gök <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a> is a theological college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, built in 1271 for the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahib-ata-fakhr-al-din-ali">Sahib Ata Fakhr al-Din Ali</a>. Its name, meaning blue madrasa, comes from the turquoise tiles of its interior. With its richly carved stone portal flanked by twin brick minarets, it is one of the finest buildings of late Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p></div>
